\par License identifier syntax
\par -------------------------
\par 
\par 1. Placement:
\par 
\par    The SPDX license identifier in OpenOCD files shall be added at the
\par    first possible line in a file which can contain a comment. For the
\par    majority of files this is the first line, except for scripts which
\par    require the '#!PATH_TO_INTERPRETER' in the first line. For those
\par    scripts the SPDX identifier goes into the second line.
\par 
\par 2. Style:
\par 
\par    The SPDX license identifier is added in form of a comment. The comment
\par    style depends on the file type::
\par 
\par       C source:  // SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression>
\par       C header:  /* SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression> */
\par       ASM:       /* SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression> */
\par       makefiles: # SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression>
\par       scripts:   # SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression>
\par       texinfo:   @c SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression>
\par       text:      # SPDX-License-Identifier: <SPDX License Expression>
\par 
\par    If a specific tool cannot handle the standard comment style, then the
\par    appropriate comment mechanism which the tool accepts shall be used. This
\par    is the reason for having the "/\\* \\*/" style comment in C header
\par    files. There was build breakage observed with generated .lds files where
\par    'ld' failed to parse the C++ comment. This has been fixed by now, but
\par    there are still older assembler tools which cannot handle C++ style
\par    comments.
\par 
\par 3. Syntax:
\par 
\par    A <SPDX License Expression> is either an SPDX short form license
\par    identifier found on the SPDX License List, or the combination of two
\par    SPDX short form license identifiers separated by "WITH" when a license
\par    exception applies. When multiple licenses apply, an expression consists
\par    of keywords "AND", "OR" separating sub-expressions and surrounded by
\par    "(", ")" .
\par 
\par    License identifiers for licenses like [L]GPL with the 'or later' option
\par    are constructed by using a "-or-later":
\par 
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
\par 
\par    WITH should be used when there is a modifier to a license needed.
\par    Exceptions can only be used with particular License identifiers. The
\par    valid License identifiers are listed in the tags of the exception text
\par    file.
\par 
\par    OR should be used if the file is dual licensed and only one license is
\par    to be selected. For example, some source files are available under dual
\par    licenses:
\par 
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-1-Clause
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-2-Clause
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-3-Clause
\par 
\par    AND should be used if the file has multiple licenses whose terms all
\par    apply to use the file. For example, if code is inherited from another
\par    project and permission has been given to put it in OpenOCD, but the
\par    original license terms need to remain in effect::
\par 
\par       // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later AND MIT
\par 
\par License identifiers
\par -------------------
\par 
\par The licenses currently used, as well as the licenses for code added to
\par OpenOCD, can be broken down into:
\par 
\par 1. `Preferred licenses`:
\par 
\par    Whenever possible these licenses should be used as they are known to be
\par    fully compatible and widely used. These licenses are available from the
\par    directory:
\par 
\par       LICENSES/preferred/
\par 
\par    in the OpenOCD source tree.
\par 
\par    The files in this directory contain the full license text and
\par    `Metatags`. The file names are identical to the SPDX license
\par    identifier which shall be used for the license in source files.
\par 
\par    Examples:
\par 
\par       LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0
\par 
\par    Contains the GPL version 2 license text and the required metatags.
\par 
\par    `Metatags`:
\par 
\par    The following meta tags must be available in a license file:
\par 
\par    - Valid-License-Identifier:
\par 
\par      One or more lines which declare which License Identifiers are valid
\par      inside the project to reference this particular license text. Usually
\par      this is a single valid identifier, but e.g. for licenses with the 'or
\par      later' options two identifiers are valid.
\par 
\par    - SPDX-URL:
\par 
\par      The URL of the SPDX page which contains additional information related
\par      to the license.
\par 
\par    - Usage-Guidance:
\par 
\par      Freeform text for usage advice. The text must include correct examples
\par      for the SPDX license identifiers as they should be put into source
\par      files according to the `License identifier syntax` guidelines.
\par 
\par    - License-Text:
\par 
\par      All text after this tag is treated as the original license text
\par 
\par    File format examples::
\par 
\par       Valid-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
\par       Valid-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
\par       Valid-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
\par       SPDX-URL: https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0.html
\par       Usage-Guide:
\par         To use this license in source code, put one of the following SPDX
\par         tag/value pairs into a comment according to the placement
\par         guidelines in the licensing rules documentation.
\par         For 'GNU General Public License (GPL) version 2 only' use:
\par           SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
\par         or
\par           SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
\par         For 'GNU General Public License (GPL) version 2 or any later version' use:
\par           SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
\par       License-Text:
\par         Full license text
\par 
\par 2. Stand-alone licenses:
\par 
\par    These licenses should only be used for stand-alone applications that are
\par    distributed with OpenOCD but are not included in the OpenOCD binary.
\par    These licenses are available from the directory:
\par 
\par      LICENSES/stand-alone/
\par 
\par    in the OpenOCD source tree.
\par 
\par    Examples:
\par 
\par      SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0
\par 
\par The format and requirements of the license files in the other sub-directories
\par of directory
\par 
\par    LICENSES
\par 
\par have to follow the same format and requirements of the `Preferred licenses`.
\par 
\par All SPDX license identifiers and exceptions must have a corresponding file
\par in the LICENSES subdirectories. This is required to allow tool
\par verification (e.g. checkpatch.pl) and to have the licenses ready to read
\par and extract right from the source, which is recommended by various FOSS
\par organizations, e.g. the `FSFE REUSE initiative <https://reuse.software/>`.
